-- title:
--   Original compensated stopped jump and HJB drift have separate L1 and signed means
-- statement:
--   For the literal Lévy process X and original dividend control D, the intrinsic stopped nonlinear source-jump compensator is integrable and centred, while the physical stopped HJB generator drift is separately integrable with nonpositive expectation. Both conclusions follow from the published original concrete compensator and signed source budget; probability and Lévy moment conditions are derived from X, not assumed. Compact predictable localisation and source drift integrability remain explicit.
-- source:
--   Source-exact combination of Proved 15ee174f and 7a07cf64; intended as a P3-E2 separate signed L1 interface for c1e2f021 and 1a1a0301.

